base-files (8) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * rc stores the networks of a wifi.txt on the boot partition with
    pie-wifi import. The import deletes the file. rc then starts pie-wifi
    watch. It gives the stored networks to each WiFi interface as it
    appears. The boot does not wait for WiFi.
  * rc's own mounts of the boot partition are root-only. One read-only
    mount serves authorized_keys and wifi.txt.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:06:20 +0000

base-files (7) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * rc starts dhcpc -a, which runs DHCP on each Ethernet interface and on
    each one that appears later.
  * Breaks dhcpc before 4, which has no -a.

